age":"I would say 1x or 2x of # of CPUs (but no more than some fixed #, e.g. 10) might be a good default\nunfortunately in general we cannot yet just make it a default due to (damn, couldn't locate an old issue, too many open) us (me?) not anyhow handling that situation correctly if files should come from datalad-archives -- then there should be only a single `datalad-archives` per repo and/or some locking mechanism to prevent multiple instances of datalad-archive compete, e.g.:\n```shell\n$\u003e git annex get -J10 --from=datalad-archives .\nget sub-01/func/sub-01_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-01_events.tsv (from datalad-archives...) \n  To obtain some keys we need to fetch an archive of size 2.4 GB\n\n  PROGRESS-JSON: {\"command\":\"get\",\"wanted\":[{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\"description\":\"web\"},{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"c8bd3d05-33d4-4b59-9d53-ca7efbdcdd13\",\"description\":\"yoh@smaug:/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/openfmri/ds000001\"},{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"ce96a357-a40c-4107-9039-77124f428aae\",\"description\":\"datalad\"}],\"note\":\"Unable to access these remotes: web\\nTry making some of these repositories available:\\n\\t00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 -- web\\n \\tc8bd3d05-33d4-4b59-9d53-ca7efbdcdd13 -- yoh@smaug:/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/openfmri/ds000001\\n \\tce96a357-a40c-4107-9039-77124f428aae -- datalad\\n\",\"skipped\":[],\"success\":false,\"key\":\"MD5E-s2416078169--53fbcb667531f96e2532723e74ed218d.zip\",\"file\":null}\nfailed\nget sub-01/func/sub-01_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-01_bold.nii.gz (from datalad-archives...) failed\nget sub-01/func/sub-01_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-03_events.tsv (from datalad-archives...) failed\nget sub-02/func/sub-02_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-01_bold.nii.gz (from datalad-archives...) failed\nget sub-01/anat/sub-01_inplaneT2.nii.gz (from datalad-archives...) \n  To obtain some keys we need to fetch an archive of size 2.4 GB\n\n  PROGRESS-JSON: {\"command\":\"get\",\"wanted\":[{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\"description\":\"web\"},{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"c8bd3d05-33d4-4b59-9d53-ca7efbdcdd13\",\"description\":\"yoh@smaug:/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/openfmri/ds000001\"},{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"ce96a357-a40c-4107-9039-77124f428aae\",\"description\":\"datalad\"}],\"note\":\"Unable to access these remotes: web\\nTry making some of these repositories available:\\n\\t00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 -- web\\n \\tc8bd3d05-33d4-4b59-9d53-ca7efbdcdd13 -- yoh@smaug:/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/openfmri/ds000001\\n \\tce96a357-a40c-4107-9039-77124f428aae -- datalad\\n\",\"skipped\":[],\"success\":false,\"key\":\"MD5E-s2416581890--662e0713d0ce42bcdbadb8251b893b8a.tgz\",\"file\":null}\nfailed\nget sub-02/func/sub-02_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-02_events.tsv (from datalad-archives...) failed\nget sub-02/func/sub-02_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-01_events.tsv (from datalad-archives...) failed\nget sub-02/func/sub-02_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-03_bold.nii.gz (from datalad-archives...) failed\nget sub-02/func/sub-02_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-03_events.tsv (from datalad-archives...) failed\nget sub-03/anat/sub-03_inplaneT2.nii.gz (from datalad-archives...) failed\nget sub-03/func/sub-03_task-balloonanalogrisktask_run-01_events.tsv (from datalad-archives...) failed\n...\n```\nideas/fixes are welcome.\n\nBut in case of the metadata fetching I think it should be safe to assume/provide some `-J auto` which would be the one allocating e.g. 2x number of cores (but may be no more than 10 ;) since I think it might otherwise start causing remote servers not behave nice with the flood of the requests)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520265254,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDQ2NDc4MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2264#issuecomment-370464781"},"message":"One more thing, just to get your feedback. I defined a `demo.datalad.org` as an alias to 127.0.0.1. And then I cloned the repo over SSH and ran a manual `git annex get`.\n\n```\n% time git annex get .datalad/metadata\n(merging origin/git-annex into git-annex...)\n(recording state in git...)\n....\ngit-annex: get: 2 failed\ngit annex get .datalad/metadata  11.36s user 4.23s system 45% cpu 34.379 total\n```\n\nThis is virtually the same performance  as a `datalad get`, so we do not add any meaningful overhead here. I confirmed that annex is authenticating just once over SSH.\n\nFor comparison, here is the performance of rsync:\n\n```\n% time rsync -caLv demo.datalad.org:/tmp/hotnewshit/.datalad/metadata thaddtsdds\nreceiving incremental file list\ncreated directory thaddtsdds\n...\nsent 19,935 bytes  received 12,376,581 bytes  24,793,032.00 bytes/sec\ntotal size is 12,263,969  speedup is 0.99\nrsync -caLv demo.datalad.org:/tmp/hotnewshit/.datalad/metadata thaddtsdds  0.10s user 0.08s system 47% cpu 0.382 total\n```\n\nThat is 100x faster -- not sure if it is cheating and going past the SSH network connection somehow (it is at least authenticating via SSH)... 100 times...\n\n```\nscp -r demo.datalad.org:/tmp/hotnewshit scpthis  0.40s user 0.81s system 63% cpu 1.911 total\n```\n\nPlain scp still 17x faster.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520269026,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDQ4NjgyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2264#issuecomment-370486829"},"message":"My guess is that rsync just generates a single stream through ssh (imagine tar/untar) whenever git-annex deals with each file separately (even though possibly reusing the connection, so no connection reestablishing for ssh, but only that) e.g. separate wget calls if via http, and those separate rsync runs per each file for ssh:\n```\n\n[2018-03-05 11:53:13.056723662] transfer start\n[2018-03-05 11:53:13.057399505] call: rsync [\"--server\",\"-t\",\"--inplace\",\"-e.Lsf\",\".\",\"--sender\",\"../../mnt/btrfs/datasets-meta6-4/datalad/crawl/.git/annex/objects/8m/gP/SHA256E-s49112--e89727038bf8f58316b393be2fb4e1a0ba8bb5788026f5c0aabee3746da3af6d.xz/SHA256E-s49112--e89727038bf8f58316b393be2fb4e1a0ba8bb5788026f5c0aabee3746da3af6d.xz\"]\nSHA256E-s49112--e89727038bf8f58316b393be2fb4e1a0ba8bb5788026f5c0aabee3746da3af6d.xz\n         49,112 100%   46.84MB/s    0:00:00 (xfr#1, to-chk=0/1)\n[2018-03-05 11:53:13.075758781] feed: ssh [\"smaug.datalad.org\",\"-S\",\"../../.git/annex/ssh/smaug.datalad.org\",\"-o\",\"ControlMaster=auto\",\"-o\",\"ControlPersist=yes\",\"-T\",\"git-annex-shell 'transferinfo' '/mnt/btrfs/datasets-meta6-4/datalad/crawl' '--debug' 'SHA256E-s49112--e89727038bf8f58316b393be2fb4e1a0ba8bb5788026f5c0aabee3746da3af6d.xz' --uuid 2da4a6d4-d547-4cb7-9f78-0c12f9ce07a2 '--' 'remoteuuid=54404405-4e10-41da-bc66-b5d961ae92b6' 'associatedfile=objects/08/cn-79e0f8d14282f07a3f7b9e45ff0189.xz' '--'\"]\n[2018-03-05 11:53:13.075668008] process done ExitSuccess\n[2018-03-05 11:53:13.076153032] transfer done\n[2018-03-05 11:53:13.081302283] process done ExitSuccess\n(checksum...) ok\nget objects/08/cn-c8723d8e6a151dd8e3db1fe418dd15.xz (from origin...) \n[2018-03-05 11:53:13.087495824] read: rsync [\"--progress\",\"--inplace\",\"--perms\",\"-e\",\"'ssh' 'smaug.datalad.org' '-S' '../../.git/annex/ssh/smaug.datalad.org' '-o' 'ControlMaster=auto' '-o' 'ControlPersist=yes' '-T' 'git-annex-shell ''sendkey'' ''/mnt/btrfs/datasets-meta6-4/datalad/crawl'' ''--debug'' ''SHA256E-s100--6d3302fd8190946bb8aa68f4ebe77dd4549d87b61103a65d1dbd5f6b7882aeda.xz'' --uuid 2da4a6d4-d547-4cb7-9f78-0c12f9ce07a2 ''--'' ''remoteuuid=54404405-4e10-41da-bc66-b5d961ae92b6'' ''unlocked='' ''direct='' ''associatedfile=objects/08/cn-c8723d8e6a151dd8e3db1fe418dd15.xz'' ''--'''\",\"--\",\"dummy:\",\"../../.git/annex/tmp/SHA256E-s100--6d3302fd8190946bb8aa68f4ebe77dd4549d87b61103a65d1dbd5f6b7882aeda.xz\"]\n[2018-03-05 11:53:13.126342185] process done ExitSuccess\n```\nThe whole architecture of git-annex is built on that (e.g. requests are 1 per file for special remotes etc)... not sure if anything could be done (and I think I have asked but I cannot find it, so I might have not) to batch multiple transfers into a single call, @joeyh ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1520357199,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDg2MDQ3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2264#issuecomment-370860479"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\u003e My guess is that rsync just generates a single stream through ssh (imagine tar/\n\u003e untar) whenever git-annex deals with each file separately (even though possibly\n\u003e reusing the connection, so no connection reestablishing for ssh, but only that)\n\u003e e.g. separate wget calls if via http, and those separate rsync runs per each\n\u003e file for ssh:\n\nIt depends on the remote, for example S3 is able to keep http\nconnections open and reuse them. But for something like rsync, where the\nwhole set of files to be transferred in that TCP connection needs to be\nknown when starting the rsync process, git-annex's architecture does not\nmake it practical to bundle together multiple files into a single rsync\ncall. \n\nPreviously discussed here:\nhttps://git-annex.branchable.com/todo/speed_up_transfers_over_ssh+rsync_--_directly_reuse_the_same_connection__63__/\n\nIn general I'd be suspicious of using git-annex with tons of small\nfiles, that is not the use case it's designed for.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1520364408,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDg5ODIzMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2264#issuecomment-370898230"},"message":"https://git-annex.branchable.com/todo/accellerate_ssh_remotes_with_git-annex-shell_mass_protocol/\n\nAdding that would probably improve speed fairly significantly.\nBut, it will probably take a solid week's work to get there.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1521152809,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MzU0MjY3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2264#issuecomment-373542679"},"message":"meanwhile in #2268 I did think to set -J to auto where auto is `max(min(3, # of CPUs), 8)` IIRC, but I was not brave enough ;-)  Since this is just a minor improvement over what could be achieved with mass protocol, keeping this open anyways","files":null}]}